# Available bitrates

Each bitrate is available as a separate revision of this repository. When planning available VRAM for kv space, refer to the appropriate VRAM column.

| BPW | Size on disk | VRAM (exllamav3) | VRAM (vLLM) | KLD |{% if show_ppl %} PPL |{% endif %}
|---|---|---|---|---|{% if show_ppl %}---|{% endif %}
{% for rev in revisions %}|[{{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(rev.bits) }}](https://huggingface.co/{{ this_model }}/tree/{{ rev.name }})|{{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(rev.disk_bytes / 1024**3) }} GiB|{{ '{0:0.2f}'.format((rev.disk_bytes-rev.embed_bytes) / 1024**3) }} GiB|{{ '{0:0.2f}'.format((rev.disk_bytes-rev.embed_bytes-rev.encoder_bytes+rev.blockq_bytes) / 1024**3) }} GiB|{{ '{0:0.4f}'.format(rev.kld) }}|{% if show_ppl %}{{ '{0:0.4f}'.format(rev.ppl) }}|{% endif %}
{% endfor %}|(base)|{{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(base_disk_bytes / 1024**3) }} GiB|||{{ '{0:0.4f}'.format(base_kld) }}|{% if show_ppl %}{{ '{0:0.4f}'.format(base_ppl) }}|{% endif %}

- BPW: Average bits per weight across tensors (not including input embeddings, encoders, or output head)
- Size on disk: Total aggregate size of tensors in checkpoint, in GiB
- VRAM (exllamav3): Total VRAM consumption as typically used in exllamav3, in GiB (minus embeddings)
- VRAM (vLLM): Total VRAM consumption as typically used in vLLM, in GiB (blockq embeddings, offloaded/omitted encoders)
- KLD: Mean KL divergence from unquantized base model at this bitrate (lower is better)
{% if show_ppl %}- PPL: Perplexity at this bitrate (lower is better)

KLD and PPL are quality metrics that represent fidelity to the base model. The values for the base model row are the noise floor: it is not possible for a quantization to meaningfully score better than this value using these metrics.{% else %}
KLD is a quality metric that represents fidelity to the base model. The value for the base model row is the noise floor: it is not possible for a quantization to meaningfully score better than this value.

Perplexity is omitted: for this model, perplexity on the raw-text test set is not meaningful even for the unquantized base model, while KLD compares against the base model directly and remains valid.{% endif %}

